        "label": "Some bright morning when this life is over",
        "syllables": "Some bright morn- ing when this life is o- ver I'll fly a- way. To that home on God's ce- les- tial shore, * I'll fly a- way. I'll fly a- way, O glo- ry, I'll fly a- way. * When I die, hal- le- lu- jah, by and by, I'll fly a- way."
      },
      {
        "label": "When the shadows of this life have gone",
        "syllables": "When the shad- ows of this life have gone, * I'll fly a- way. Like a bird from pris- on bars have flown, * I'll fly a- way. I'll fly a- way, O glo- ry, I'll fly a- way. * When I die, hal- le- lu- jah, by and by, I'll fly a- way."
      },
      {
        "label": "Just a few more weary days and then",
        "syllables": "Just a few more wea- ry days and then, * I'll fly a- way. To a land where joy will ne- ver end, * I'll fly a- way. I'll fly a- way, O glo- ry, I'll fly a- way. * When I die, hal- le- lu- jah, by and by, I'll fly a- way."
      }
    ]
  },
